WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got a bulldog named Tank.
-I did. I did.

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.005
And here´s a picture Tank.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
Adorable.
-Oh, she is so sweet.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.976
-And how is life with Tank?
You did not have Tank last time

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were here.
-I didn´t.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:14.981
It took me a while to get Tank.
-Mm-hmm, ´cause you were -- why?

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don´t know.
I was procrastinating.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.418
-Was it someone else´s dog?

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was worried.

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:24.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was worried about
an animal in my home.

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
So -- but I got Tank,

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she´s really --
she´s an odd dog.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:32.165
I mean, she´s as odd as you
would imagine her to be, my dog.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why -- oh, your --
because it´s your dog?

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guess so.
I don´t know.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.470 size:84% position:42%
I mean -- I don´t know.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s true.
I wouldn´t expect --

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But she´s very --
she´s very vocal.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Vocal. Now, a dog --
do you mean they´re barking

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot?
-Yes.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
She barks a lot,
but she makes --

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.215
she makes really weird noises.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She makes weird noises?
-Yeah, I think she --

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.819
she´ll be like, she kind of
talks a little bit to me.

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You brought a video.
Are you gonna --

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.322
should we try to hear what
you think Tank is saying?

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. I just -- no.
I was seeing where that

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
was going.
No, let´s just watch the --

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
let´s watch the Tank.
-All right.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:03.997 size:88% position:44%
Let´s hear Tank talking.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Dog growling ]

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:07.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I love you.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love you.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.805
[ Dog growls "I love you" ]

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:15.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience awws ]

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.343 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why -- what --
I mean, I feel like --

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:22.649
-Yes, yes, they´re clapping!

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why?

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like you
should retire and let --

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.222
-I know.
-Tank should be the breadwinner.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know! I know!
-How is Tank not on TV?

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.460
He´s the "I love you" dog.
-I don´t know, it´s just crazy.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
She needs her own
YouTube channel or something.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s -- that happened.
That´s real.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.199
-How do you -- by the way,
because -- and I don´t want

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:43.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
to judge you, but I --
like, what made you think that

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:44.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
that would work?

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I have a dog too,
and I never said, "You know,

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:49.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m gonna try to get it to say
´I love you´ back."

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you were in a situation
where it worked.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.314
-She -- she makes these noises.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:57.684
-She makes kind of noises
like -- like you heard.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
And kind of, if you say
a word before it,

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.288 size:78% position:39%
it sounds like that´s
what she´s saying.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:05.091
So, if you say, like, "hello,"
it sounds like she´s saying,

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
"ewwo."

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:11.498 size:84% position:42%
And there was this time
where I was upstairs

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:15.068
and she peed on my friend´s rug.
You know, so we put her away.

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:18.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And -- and then I left,

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.772 size:81% position:41%
you know, but the dog
was alone in the room.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
And apparently it sounded like
she was saying "I´m --

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m sorry."

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
My friend was so,
like, freaked out.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:28.181
And she was like, "The dog´s in
there going ´I´m sorry!

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:32.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I´m sor-Ry!´"

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are --
-And she was so flipped out.

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.323
And -- anyway.
-There are so many things there

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
that make you the world´s
worst house guest.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You bring your dog.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-It pisses on a rug.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then you´re like,
"I´m gonna take off.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way, she talks."
-Oh, I know.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:50.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know. I know.
I did get a new rug.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that´s very nice.
-And I cleaned it.

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.073 size:84% position:42%
-Oh, that was -- you --
-It was a small rug.

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That seems like you did
two things that are redundant.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The dog peed.
-I feel like, either clean

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
the rug or got a new one.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But get a new one
and clean one --

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did both.
I tried to.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:02.649 size:84% position:42%
-Now I take it back.
You´re the world´s best

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:03.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
house guest.
-Yeah.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
Neither one worked very well.
-Another thing we --

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:08.221
I gave you a hard time about
before, and I want to apologize,

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:11.324
is that you admitted to us that
on your acting resumé,

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:13.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
on your headshot,
your special skill, you listed

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
that driving was
a special skill.

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:16.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-You thought that that would

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:19.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
separate you from the pack
´cause they would say,

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.969
"We´re down to two actresses,
but only one of them drives."

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, but then -- and I thought
that was, you know,

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
pretty exceptional,
that you would think that

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:32.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was worth noting.
But you also, you had another

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
time, you wrote,
as a special skill,

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you could run
long distances.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:39.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that true?
-No.

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
No. I don´t --
and I was reminded of that.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It clearly was on there.
-Yes.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was remind--
-So, you can´t even do it.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Wow.

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:53.132
-No, I mean -- like most people,
I can run short distances,

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:56.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
particularly if I´m
uncomfortable or scared.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. Got it.
-You know.

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.372
-Again, not a special skill.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.042
Or even -- or even a skill.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
I do not know --

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I run when I´m scared."
"Oh, wow.

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:09.382
Did you go to school for that?"
-Right.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:12.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. I don´t know.
I was -- I just remembered

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:15.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
that backstage, I had --
I can´t remember doing that.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.157
-What kind of part did you think
that would be helpful for?

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don´t know.
I mean, I imagine if they were

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
remaking, like, "Marathon Man"
or something like that.

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But even then,
I would like to point out,

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you should know this, too.
Because in movies,

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don´t have to show all
of the running.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.304 size:81% position:41%
You know, you just run
a little bit and then

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:33.640 size:78% position:39%
they edit it together
and it looks like --

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.475
You run a little bit here,
and then they cut to you running

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.043 size:81% position:41%
somewhere else and as
a viewer you go, "Wow,

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:39.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
they ran a long way."
But an actor --

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My God.
Maybe -- I don´t know what.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:45.918
I mean, like, that they thought,
you know, "She has endurance.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:48.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
She can go the distance."
-Oh, I see.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.923
-She can work long days.
We´re not going to make her run,

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
but she has --
-She has endurance.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.129
-And obviously, it´s worked.
You´ve been very successful.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.097
-I mean, yeah, in some way.
-But, because they´re like --

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.233
I mean, they´re sort of --
I think it´s just, someone looks

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
and goes, "Oh."
-Maybe that was

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:02.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
in theatre school.
Maybe I still was

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:05.204
in theatre school coming up
with things that I thought

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:08.007
big Hollywood people would like,
like driving and --

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
long-distance running.
-It feels like, then we should

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:12.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
blame your theatre school that
didn´t teach you those

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:14.547
weren´t important things.

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.916
I think what you wanted them
to know was, "Look, I can drive,

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.319
but if there isn´t a car,
I could also run there."

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:21.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:24.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was I thinking?
And also, when --

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
when did I say that out loud,
in public?

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:29.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then it was on the Internet,
you know what I mean?

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:31.164
-Yeah, ´cause we -- our
researchers found in real life.

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:33.399
But you put it there,
and then instead of just burying

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
the memory you then,
at some point, admitted it.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:37.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-You know, I think you´re,

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
at your core,
a very honest person.

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:41.207
And no matter how much you like
to hide things, you eventually

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:43.309
admit that you talked to
your dog until it told you

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:45.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it loved you.

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:47.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think you´re right.
I think there´s some truth

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
to that.
-And -- this is very exciting.

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys are gonna do
a seventh season.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re back to work now.
-Yes.

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:53.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is just thrilling.
-Yeah.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And -- we were
talking backstage.

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:58.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not only is that an
incredible accomplishment,

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.460 size:84% position:42%
to be on seven years.
But, at the very least,

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:03.663
it means you´re gonna come back
here for a sixth time.

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:05.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m just so happy
in advance to have you back.

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:07.467 size:78% position:39%
-Oh, what a pleasure.

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:08.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:11.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´m sure we´ll have more
talking dog videos.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.739 size:84% position:42%
Oh, yeah. by the way,
the next time you come,

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:14.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
it´s got to be, like,
a full sentence.

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:15.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-I mean, like, I know

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:18.044
"I love you" is a full sentence,
but, like, something really --

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, I´ll work on it.
-A shopping list.

00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:21.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want you to say, "I´m going
to the grocery store.

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:22.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you need anything?"
-Okay.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:23.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want Tank to say
at least four --

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Aluminum foil!"

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:28.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:29.856 size:84% position:42%
-Give it up, everybody,
for Taylor Schilling!

